<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lat Sukaabe Fall</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1719">1719</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lat Sukaabe Fall was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolof">Wolof</a> ruler who united the thrones of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cayor">Cayor</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baol">Baol</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> around 1697, taking the combined title of damel-teigne. He strengthened royal power with firearms and slave soldiers and dealt with the French trading posts on the coast. His descendants dominated Cayor and Baol until the 19th century.</p></div>
